dxgi: Report half of the GPU's working set as the video memory budget, with unified memory.

QueryVideoMemoryInfo() reported recommendedMaxWorkingSetSize, the most the GPU should
hold, as the budget. With unified memory that is three quarters of the memory of the whole
system: 17.8 GB on a 24 GB Mac. A game plans its texture streaming by the budget (Call of
Duty: WWII registers for its changes), and one that fills it leaves too little for itself and
the system, which then compresses and swaps. Call of Duty: WWII grew to 18 GB in a mission,
7.4 GB of the system went to swap, and its frame rate fell from 120 to under 50 with the GPU
idle part of each frame.

The budget is now what the adapter already reports as its DedicatedVideoMemory, half of the
working set with unified memory. DXMT_VIDEO_MEMORY_BUDGET_MB sets another.

LOCAL TO THIS PORT, NOT FOR DXMT. Applied by macos/build-dxmt.sh to
github.com/athei/dxmt at 01e59e9bde030f105937f249afaac92ada01b4d7, after 0001 and 0002.
Written with an AI assistant (Claude). DXMT does not accept contributions made or
co-authored by AI (its CONTRIBUTING.md), so this patch must not be sent to it as a pull
